A **tangent** is a straight line that touches the circumference at exactly one point and does not enter the circle.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[thick] (O) circle (2.6);
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\draw (-2.6,0) -- (2.6,0) node[pos=0.76,sloped,above] {diameter};
\draw (250:2.6) -- (O) node[midway,sloped,above] {radius};
\draw (25:2.6) -- (95:2.6) node[midway,sloped,below] {chord};
\draw ($(145:2.6)+(235:1.5)$) -- ($(145:2.6)+(55:1.5)$);
\node at (0.75,-0.4) {centre};
\node at (-2.1,3.3) {tangent};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0.2,-2.95) -- (285:2.65);
\node[below] at (0.2,-3.0) {circumference};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A **segment** is the region between a chord and an arc.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[thick] (O) circle (2);
\fill (O) circle (1.6pt);
\draw (O) -- (30:2);
\draw (O) -- (130:2);
\draw[very thick] (30:2) arc[start angle=30,end angle=130,radius=2];
\node at (80:1.3) {sector};
\node at (80:2.35) {arc};
\coordinate (P) at (5,0);
\draw[thick] (P) circle (2);
\fill (P) circle (1.6pt);
\draw ($(P)+(205:2)$) -- ($(P)+(335:2)$) node[midway,above] {chord};
\node at (5,-1.42) {segment};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

